// Preflight: one document that exercises everything reported broken, so a
// build can be LOOKED AT before it is handed over. Not a sample — it is
// deliberately ugly and exhaustive.

@h1 Heading one
@h2 Heading two
@h3 Heading three
@h4 Heading four
@h5 Heading five
@h6 Heading six

#### Four hashes, which is a heading too

Prose with **bold**, *italic*, `code` and ==highlight==.
A second line, which should be a second line.

@quote A quote must never be a dark box, whatever the editor thinks.

@h6 Divider: line, dots, wave

@divider

@divider style=dots

@divider style=wave

@panel
  (accent=alert title="Parameters on the line below")
  Body text under them.

@panel(title="Parameters inline")
  Body text.

@table Q4
  Area, Owner, Notes
  Search, Ana, "one \n two"
  Export, Ben, single line

@timeline title="Four events, one with a forced break"
  Q3 2026: Discovery
    twelve interviews
  Oct 2026: **Alpha**\n release
  Dec 2026: Beta
  Q1 2027: Launch

@matrix(x="Effort" y="Impact" title="Two by two")
  Search\n relevance at tr
  Export at bl

@journey title="Stages, one broken"
  stage Discover\n and read feeling=happy
  stage Install feeling=frustrated
  stage Use feeling=neutral

@note a margin note, in handwriting

@pagebreak label="Appendix"

@h2 After the break
